    "finding": "Complete-expansion diffusion obtains U/V gradient rows with the same face argument, builds the entire tensor, then transposes it. Boundary Taylor expansions may be solved as a coupled gradient/trace system. MOOSE singularity fallback to one-term expansion is NOT transplanted. No external code copied to product."
  },
  "designRequirements": [
    "One vector face-stress operator must return the physical integrated flux and its complete sparse derivative/coefficient map, including cross-component and nonlocal wall DOFs; scalar momentum and forces consume it.",
    "Pressure-velocity response and preconditioning must correspond to the actual extracted operator. High-order polynomial reproduction alone cannot establish positive scalar rAU or a stable fixed-point map.",
    "Boundary trace semantics use actual polygon normals/face centres, with constant vs smooth trace derivatives explicit. Circle exact-field traction residual must identify incompatibility with prescribed polygon traces.",
    "Wall divergence constraints cannot be used to cancel normal stresses without physical-case validation; the simplest such projection doubled coarse pressure error here.",
    "The shared FlowEquation kernel proposed by root is appropriate to make these operator contracts testable; these wall prototypes do not justify changing defaults."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "No spatial-accuracy qualification or stability repair demonstrated on6208 cells by these wall candidates.",
    "Runtime costs overlap the parent build and concurrent work, so are not isolation performance comparisons.",
    "Native circle traction audits have prescribed-polygon boundary mismatch; exact smooth-trace case is reconstruction consistency only.",
    "The prototype paired U/V hook exists solely because old scalar momentum API omits the other component; do not ship it.",
    "No larger mesh chain or DFG tests started."
  ],
